      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine how far Jana can walk in 10 minutes, given that she takes 24 minutes to walk one mile.\n\n1. **Determine the walking rate:**\n   Jana's walking rate (in miles per minute) is calculated by dividing the distance she walks by the time it takes for that distance.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Walking rate} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Set up a proportion:**\n   We need to find out how far she will walk in 10 minutes. Let \\( x \\) be the distance in miles she walks in 10 minutes.\n\n   We use the ratio of the walking rate:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ minutes}} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\( x \\):**\n   To find \\( x \\), we set up the equation and solve for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   x \\text{ miles} = \\left( \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}} \\right) \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x \\text{ miles} = \\frac{10}{24} \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the fraction:**\n   Simplify the fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{10}{24} = \\frac{5}{12} \\approx 0.416666...\n   \\]\n\n5. **Round to the nearest tenth:**\n   To express the distance to the nearest tenth:\n   \\[\n   0.416666... \\approx 0.4\n   \\]\n\n6. **Final Answer:**\n   Strip off the '0.400...' part and write it closely:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{0.4}\n   \\]",
